## Unicode Character Database — `src/casefold.zig`

`src/casefold.zig` is the simple case-folding relation of Unicode 17.0.0
(`CaseFolding.txt`, status C and S entries); it is generated by
`tools/ucd_unicode` from the UCD files and compiled into the module (it is what `(?i)` matches by). It is a TRANSFORMED
form of the data, not a copy of the file: the relation is re-encoded as runs
of orbit successors (`lo`, `hi`, `delta` or alternating pairs). The Unicode
License v3 permits modification; the notice below is reproduced because its
clause (a) asks that it appear with all copies of the Data Files.

## Unicode Character Database — `src/unicode_tables.zig`

`src/unicode_tables.zig` is the General_Category, Script,
Script_Extensions, Age, the binary properties, Grapheme_Cluster_Break,
Word_Break and Sentence_Break properties of Unicode 17.0.0 (with their
aliases, `PropertyAliases.txt` and `PropertyValueAliases.txt`); it is
generated by `tools/ucd_unicode` from the UCD files, by the rules of Rust's
`regex-syntax` (checked against that crate on Unicode 16.0.0), and compiled
into the module
(it is what `\p{…}` and the Unicode `\w \s \d` match by). It is a
TRANSFORMED form of the data, not a copy of the files: each class is
re-encoded as code-point ranges in LEB128 varints. The same licence and
notice apply.

